// Recon tool run with lookalike characters
//
// Fires when a built-in recon tool runs with characters outside Latin-1 in its command line.
// ArgFuscator found that nltest, wmic, ipconfig, netstat, route and AdFind accept lookalikes,
// like a fullwidth letter or a Unicode slash. So "nltest /ｄomain_trusts" still works and
// walks right past rules that match plain text. French accents like é, à and ç are inside
// Latin-1 and don't trigger it.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  High
// MITRE:     T1027.010
// Tables:    DeviceProcessEvents
// Custom details: AccountName, FileName
//
// Needs:
//   - Nothing beyond Defender for Endpoint.
//
// Heads up: a command pasted from Word or Outlook can carry a smart quote or an en dash and
// will fire. It's easy to spot in the command line. Names outside Latin-1 fire too, like a
// Cyrillic, Greek, Polish or Turkish group name. If your directory uses those, exclude the
// names or skip this rule.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Look at the command line for the odd characters.
//   - Escalate if they're lookalike letters or slashes. Nobody types those by accident.
//   - Close if it's a smart quote or dash pasted from a document.
//
// Based on: ArgFuscator's models for nltest, wmic, ipconfig, netstat, route and adfind.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where FileName matches regex @'(?i)^(?:net1?|nltest|whoami|ipconfig|netstat|route|arp|nbtstat|systeminfo|hostname|tasklist|query|quser|qwinsta|qprocess|wmic|nslookup|cmdkey|klist|setspn|dsquery|gpresult|adfind)\.exe$' or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName matches regex @'(?i)^(?:net1?|nltestrk|whoami|ipconfig|netstat|sysinfo|tasklist|quser|qwinsta|wmic|nslookup|cmdkey|setspn|dsquery|gprslt|adfind)\.exe(?:\.mui)?$'
| where ProcessCommandLine matches regex @'[^\x00-\xff]'
| project Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountDomain, AccountName, AccountSid, FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessParentFileName
